# ==============================================================================
# Git attributes — Unity project
# Normalizes line endings and routes large binary assets through Git LFS.
# NOTE: Run `git lfs install` once per machine before cloning/committing binaries.
# ==============================================================================

# Auto-detect text files, normalize to LF in the repo
* text=auto

# Unity YAML files — force LF and mark as text so meta/scene/prefab merges work
*.cs        text diff=csharp
*.shader    text
*.cginc     text
*.hlsl      text
*.uss       text
*.uxml      text
*.json      text
*.md        text
*.asmdef    text
*.meta      text

# --- Git LFS: deliberately not used ---
#
# The LFS filters that used to live here are gone, and they are gone because they
# actively caused a bug rather than preventing one.
#
# *.png was routed through LFS, so MainMenuBackground.png and HudReference.png were
# committed as 131-byte pointer files whose objects were never pushed. Both CI jobs
# already pass `lfs: true` and still received the stubs. Unity imported the text as a
# texture without complaining, and MainMenu.uss's background-image resolved to nothing -
# a title screen with no artwork and no error anywhere explaining why.
#
# Beyond that the free tier is 1 GB of storage and 1 GB of bandwidth per month, which one
# texture pack exhausts, and the failure mode when it runs out is another silent pointer.
#
# Binary assets come through Tools/Assets/fetch-assets.py instead: declared in
# Tools/Assets/manifest.json with a licence and a SHA-256, downloaded in CI, cached, and
# never committed. The repository stores the recipe, not the output - the same reasoning
# that keeps scenes as generators.
#
# Tools/CompileCheck/check-lfs-pointers.py fails the build if a pointer ever reappears.
